Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 18:06:53 -0500
Subject: Re: AI for code

Hey so I woke up today and decided that I *still*
didn't like having AI-generated code authored under
my name.  So I rebased and split out that hunk
specifically to attribute Claude, and extracted the
relevant transcript with Claude in the commit notes.

It was an exercise in using jq without consulting
AI to do a quick-and-dirty job... but it is one that
is worth it I think. :)  In any case, "git blame" on
xlib/tree-search.pl is not as misleading as it used
to be.  and i feel much more confident writing code!
